---
import V9Layout from '~/layouts/V9Layout.astro';
import Content from '~/components/v9/content/Content.astro';
import { publicLinks } from '~/data/v9/preview-links';
import { fetchPosts } from '~/utils/blog';
import { getPermalink } from '~/utils/permalinks';
const post = (await fetchPosts()).find((post) => post.slug === 'blog/signal-vs-noise-technical-hiring')!;

const shareUrl = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, 'https://www.tribera.ai').href;
---

<V9Layout
  title="Signal versus noise: tribera"
  description="Most hiring teams spend their week evaluating people who should never have entered the process."
  headerLinkOverrides={publicLinks}
  footerLinkOverrides={publicLinks}
  openGraphType="article"
  image="~/assets/images/blog/signal-based-hiring.png"
>
  <Content kind="article">
    <div class="reading" aria-hidden="true"><span class="reading__f"></span></div>

    <header class="ahead band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="ahead__meta">
          <time datetime={post.publishDate.toISOString()}
            >{
              post.publishDate.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
                day: 'numeric',
                month: 'short',
                year: 'numeric',
                timeZone: 'UTC',
              })
            }</time
          ><i>·</i>
          {post.category && <a href={getPermalink(post.category.slug, 'category')}>{post.category.title}</a>}<i>·</i
          ><span>{post.readingTime} read</span>
        </p>
        <h1>Signal versus noise</h1>
        <p class="ahead__sub">Why clarity drives speed, and why most teams have it backwards.</p>
        <div class="ahead__by">
          <span class="ahead__ph" id="byPh" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="ahead__who"><b>Akshata Chandavarkar</b>Founder &amp; CEO</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="band band--w">
      <div class="wrap">
        <article class="art">
          <p class="lede">
            Most hiring teams are not slow because they are careless. They are slow because they are evaluating the
            wrong people, carefully.
          </p>

          <p>
            Watch where the hours actually go on an open role. A small number go into deciding between strong
            candidates, which is the work. The rest goes into establishing that people were never going to be right, a
            determination that gets made in round two, by a senior engineer, at forty minutes a time.
          </p>

          <p>
            That is not a speed problem. It is a clarity problem wearing a speed problem’s clothes, and buying a faster
            process will not touch it.
          </p>

          <h2>Noise is expensive at the wrong end</h2>

          <p>
            A weak candidate at the top of a funnel costs four minutes. The same candidate at round two costs four
            people an hour each, plus the scheduling, plus the slow erosion of your hiring managers' willingness to take
            the pipeline seriously.
          </p>

          <p>
            That last cost is the one nobody measures and the one that does the most damage. A manager who has seen six
            unsuitable people in a row starts skimming, and skimming is when good candidates get missed.
          </p>

          <blockquote class="pull">
            Noise does not just waste time.
            <em>It teaches your team to stop paying attention.</em>
          </blockquote>

          <h2>Clarity has to happen before sourcing, not after</h2>

          <p>
            The fix is unglamorous. Write down what good looks like, four or five dimensions, weighted, agreed with the
            hiring manager, before the first CV arrives. A bar written after the first CV is a description of that CV.
          </p>

          <p>
            Everything downstream gets cheaper. Screening has something to screen against. Interviewers know which
            dimension they own. And the ranking at the end is a comparison rather than an argument, because everyone was
            measuring the same thing.
          </p>

          <p>
            It takes forty-five minutes at the start and it is the highest-leverage forty-five minutes in the whole
            process. Almost nobody spends it.
          </p>

          <p class="signoff">Belong. Build. Become.</p>
        </article>
        <div class="aft">
          <div class="atags">
            {
              post.tags?.map((tag) => (
                <a class="atag" href={getPermalink(tag.slug, 'tag')}>
                  {tag.title}
                </a>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <div class="ashare">
            <span>Share</span><a
              href={`https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=${encodeURIComponent(shareUrl)}`}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
            ><a href={shareUrl} data-copy-article>Permalink</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap band" id="related">
      <div class="shead" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;text-align:center;justify-items:center;gap:8px">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--red" data-v9-reveal>Keep reading</p>
          <h2 class="h2" data-v9-reveal style="--d:60ms;max-width:none;margin-bottom:clamp(16px,2vw,24px)">
            Three more that came out of real mandates.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="dek" data-v9-reveal style="--d:100ms;max-width:none">
          Or go back to <a
            href="/blog"
            style="color:var(--red);
    text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(218,0,7,.35)"
            >everything we’ve published</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rel" data-v9-reveal style="--d:140ms">
        <a class="relc" href="/blog/rethinking-hiring-metrics-signal-efficiency"
          ><p class="relc__k">Hiring strategy</p><p class="relc__t">Rethinking hiring metrics</p><p class="relc__x">
            Time-to-hire measures your speed. Interview-to-hire measures your aim.
          </p></a
        ><a class="relc" href="/blog/designing-for-trust-privacy-transparency-respect"
          ><p class="relc__k">Candidate experience</p><p class="relc__t">Designing for trust</p><p class="relc__x">
            Most people looking for a job already have one.
          </p></a
        ><a class="relc" href="/blog/designing-ai-for-high-stakes-technical-assessment"
          ><p class="relc__k">AI and assessment</p><p class="relc__t">Designing AI for high-stakes assessment</p><p
            class="relc__x"
          >
            A model can read a transcript. It cannot tell you whether the person meant it.
          </p></a
        >
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trust band" id="cta">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="sub" style="text-align:center;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center">
          <p class="sub__k">Newsletter in preparation</p>
          <p class="sub__h">Get notified when it is ready.</p>
          <p class="sub__s">Leave your email and we will send one note when the field notes newsletter opens.</p>
          <form
            class="apply__form"
            data-newsletter-form
            action="/.netlify/functions/site-inquiry"
            method="post"
            enctype="multipart/form-data"
            style="display:flex;justify-content:center;width:fit-content;margin-inline:auto"
          >
            <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="newsletter" /><input
              type="hidden"
              name="form_loaded_at"
            /><input
              type="text"
              name="botcheck"
              tabindex="-1"
              autocomplete="off"
              aria-hidden="true"
              style="position:absolute;left:-9999px"
            />
            <div class="apply__row apply__row--2">
              <input
                class="apply__mail"
                type="email"
                name="email"
                required
                placeholder="your@email.com"
                aria-label="Your email address"
              />
              <button class="apply__go" type="submit" disabled>Notify me<span class="apply__ar">→</span></button>
            </div>
          </form>
          <noscript
            ><p class="apply__fine">
              For updates, email <a href="mailto:hello@tribera.ai?subject=Field%20notes%20notifications"
                >hello@tribera.ai</a
              >.
            </p></noscript
          ><p class="apply__fine" data-newsletter-status aria-live="polite">We never share the list.</p><script
            src="/scripts/newsletter-signup.js"
            defer></script>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band band--w close" id="contact">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="shead" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;text-align:center;justify-items:center;gap:8px">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--red" data-v9-reveal>Two doors</p>
            <h2 class="h2" data-v9-reveal style="max-width:none">Two doors. Same room.</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="dek" data-v9-reveal style="--d:60ms;max-width:none">
            If you have a role you’re stuck on, or you’re the one being interviewed, both of those start the same way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="doors" data-v9-reveal style="--d:110ms">
          <div class="door">
            <p class="door__k">If you’re hiring</p>
            <p class="door__t">Three names you’d take any of.</p>
            <p class="door__d">
              A hundred signals, a senior expert on each shortlisted person, and the reasoning behind every rank.
            </p>
            <p class="door__next"><span>Next</span> A 45-minute intake call. Three names back inside 36 hours.</p>
            <a href="/" class="btn btn--dark">See how one role ran</a>
          </div>
          <div class="door">
            <p class="door__k">If you’re looking</p>
            <p class="door__t">One conversation, then teams come to you.</p>
            <p class="door__d">
              Half an hour with someone who has done your job. Anonymous until you decide otherwise.
            </p>
            <p class="door__next"><span>Next</span> Fifteen minutes to set up, and you keep the score.</p>
            <a href="/candidates" class="btn btn--ghost">Create your profile</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="bbb2" data-v9-reveal><span>Belong</span><i></i><span>Build</span><i></i><span>Become</span></p>
        <p class="bbb2__s" data-v9-reveal>Tribe + Era. A hire only works if both sides were right about each other.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <script>
      /* ══ INDUSTRIES: the same six dimensions, any two sectors ══ */
      (function () {
        const W = {
          'consumer-digital-commerce': { n: 'Consumer & digital commerce', w: [30, 24, 8, 22, 6, 10] },
          'banking-financial-services': { n: 'Banking & financial services', w: [20, 14, 30, 10, 18, 8] },
          'enterprise-technology': { n: 'Enterprise technology', w: [26, 26, 10, 20, 10, 8] },
          'product-saas': { n: 'Product & SaaS', w: [22, 18, 6, 20, 8, 26] },
          'ai-data': { n: 'AI & data', w: [30, 26, 10, 16, 10, 8] },
          cybersecurity: { n: 'Cybersecurity', w: [24, 16, 32, 12, 10, 6] },
          'healthcare-life-sciences': { n: 'Healthcare & life sciences', w: [18, 12, 30, 10, 22, 8] },
          pharmaceutical: { n: 'Pharmaceutical', w: [16, 10, 34, 8, 24, 8] },
          manufacturing: { n: 'Manufacturing', w: [22, 14, 22, 18, 14, 10] },
          'industrial-engineering': { n: 'Industrial & engineering', w: [24, 18, 18, 18, 14, 8] },
          'global-capability-centres': { n: 'Global capability centres', w: [22, 18, 12, 20, 10, 18] },
          'private-equity-portfolio': { n: 'Private equity portfolio', w: [20, 14, 10, 32, 8, 16] },
        };
        const D = [
          'Core depth',
          'Systems design',
          'Controls and risk',
          'Delivery speed',
          'Documentation',
          'Stakeholder handling',
        ];
        const a = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#secA'),
          b = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#secB'),
          ft = document.getElementById('cmpFt');
        if (!a || !b) return;
        function paint() {
          if (!a || !b || !ft) return;
          const A = W[a.value],
            B = W[b.value];
          let mx = 0,
            gap = -1,
            gi = 0;
          D.forEach(function (_, i) {
            mx = Math.max(mx, A.w[i], B.w[i]);
            const g = Math.abs(A.w[i] - B.w[i]);
            if (g > gap) {
              gap = g;
              gi = i;
            }
          });
          D.forEach(function (n, i) {
            {
              const node = document.getElementById('fa' + i);
              if (node) node.style.width = (A.w[i] / mx) * 100 + '%';
            }
            {
              const node = document.getElementById('fb' + i);
              if (node) node.style.width = (B.w[i] / mx) * 100 + '%';
            }
            {
              const node = document.getElementById('va' + i);
              if (node) node.textContent = A.w[i];
            }
            {
              const node = document.getElementById('vb' + i);
              if (node) node.textContent = B.w[i];
            }
            {
              const node = document.getElementById('bw' + i);
              if (node) node.classList.toggle('key', i === gi);
            }
          });
          if (A.n === B.n) {
            ft.innerHTML = 'Same sector both sides. <b>Pick two and the bar moves.</b>';
            return;
          }
          ft.innerHTML =
            '<b>' +
            D[gi] +
            '</b> moves from ' +
            Math.min(A.w[gi], B.w[gi]) +
            '% to ' +
            Math.max(A.w[gi], B.w[gi]) +
            '% — a ' +
            gap +
            '-point swing, and <b>a different person wins</b>.';
        }
        a.addEventListener('change', paint);
        b.addEventListener('change', paint);
        paint();
      })();
    </script>
  </Content>
</V9Layout>
